==Strategy==
This stage is nearly impossible without all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] due to the [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]]' high buffs. Because of this, it is highly recommended you max them out for the highest chance of success. Even then, the buffs can make this stage extremely difficult, especially with several Mesocosmocyclones and a dangerous Professor A. as supports.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] - An obvious choice for this stage given its Warp Immunity and Strong against [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]]. It is vulnerable against Professor A. though.
*[[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] - Can slow both the Mesocosmocyclones and Super Cosmic Cyclone, making him a valuable crowd-controller here.
*[[Ancient Egg: N105 (Rare Cat)|Racquet Cat]] - Surprisingly useful here, since she can knockback the Mesocosmocyclones, and can actually outrange Super Cosmic Cyclone unlike Seafarer. Be careful about sending her out too much, since she can push into Professor A.'s range if not careful.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - Deals high damage and can earn extra cash through [[Talents]]. If the Target Alien Talent is also obtained, they can slow down the Mesocosmocyclones too.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - Freezes the Mesocosmocyclones, though can't hit Super Cosmic Cyclone.
*[[Adult Cat (Rare Cat)|Prisoner Cat]] - Useful for hitting Professor A. out from behind Super Cosmic Cyclone. Beware his frailty and long recharge time.
*[[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] - Can be stacked at the beginning to snipe Professor A. easily. Resistant to Aliens, so can take a lot of warps from the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclones]].
*[[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]] - Usual issues with survivability are solved by Super Cosmic Cyclone's constant Warping. Cat God is capable of knocking back and dealing great damage to the entire field, including the Professor A.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]] - Very high damage and health against Professor A., though she has the stats to work as a generalist backliner for the whole stage.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]] - High damage and a long piercing range, with both targeted traits being the main threats of the level, make her a very powerful unit. Her short recharge time lets her be stacked easily, and she will be able to take care of Professor A. quickly.
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]]/[[Sweet Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Chocoladite]] - With Massive Damage against Alien and [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies respectively, both do an adequate job at whittling down the Cosmic Cyclones, as well as the Professor A.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]] - With [[Insane Damage]] against the main threats of this stage, Izanagi completely annihilates the Professor A. using Super Cosmic Cyclone as a stepping stone.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]] - With the ability to [[Freeze]] both Alien and Red enemies while also being [[Strong]], as well as [[Explosion]] and a quick cooldown to boot, she is able to put a complete stop to both threats as she is well able to hit what's behind the Cyclone.

